- [Host] Thanks to Indochino

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:02.820
for keeping Legal Eagle in the air

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:04.523
and helping me look fly.

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:09.103
Hey Legal Eagles

00:00:09.103 --> 00:00:10.887
it's time to think like a lawyer.

00:00:10.887 --> 00:00:12.310
And I'm incredibly excited

00:00:12.310 --> 00:00:15.800
to have the famous
hbomberguy with us today.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:16.980
Why don't we talk a little bit

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:18.290
about your channel itself.
- Okay.

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:21.050
- [Host] You have just
exploded in popularity

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:25.200
as being some of the best
social commentary on YouTube

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.647
and one of the best Donkey Kong players--

00:00:27.647 --> 00:00:28.480
- (laughs)

00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:29.850
- [Host] I suppose is out there.

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:31.150
- Well technically I'm one of the worst

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:32.770
I just eventually managed to do it.

00:00:32.770 --> 00:00:35.623
- Well depends on what
the ultimate goal is.

00:00:35.623 --> 00:00:36.730
- [Harry] (laughs)
- Is it to beat the game

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:39.480
or is it to do it in a
very very difficult way

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.520
in the most amusing way possible.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.080
- I guess it's that yeah.

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:45.010
- Well one thing I think was amazing

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:46.986
is I guess AOC commented

00:00:46.986 --> 00:00:49.424
on your live stream right?
- Yeah yeah.

00:00:49.424 --> 00:00:51.259
People were joking about getting her on

00:00:51.259 --> 00:00:53.400
and I thought ah that's quite fun.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.850
But then an account that was AOC

00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:57.910
joined the call and it
was actually her voice

00:00:57.910 --> 00:00:59.850
and I lost my mind.

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:00.970
- [Alexandra] Hello?

00:01:00.970 --> 00:01:01.803
- [Harry] Hi.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:03.700
It's fantastic to meet you.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:04.700
Would you like to introduce yourself

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:06.600
in case some people
don't know who you are?

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:10.100
- [Alexandra] Oh my name is
Alexandria Ocasio Cortez.

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:11.530
I am the congresswoman

00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:14.060
for New York's 14th
congressional district.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:15.900
And now like Bernie
Sanders is doing streaming.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:17.880
So I feel like people are following suit.

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:19.050
I started a trend

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:22.070
in left wing American politics by accident

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:23.270
while trying to make fun

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:25.720
of a former comedian in Britain.

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:27.130
But these things happen.

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:29.586
- And how much did you raise for charity?

00:01:29.586 --> 00:01:31.913
- About $330,000.
- [Host] That's incredible.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:35.829
So what kind of legal questions

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:38.640
can I help answer for you.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:40.896
- Well I was wondering on behalf

00:01:40.896 --> 00:01:42.900
of semi-political YouTubers

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:47.460
how can one broach

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:49.380
important and contentious topics

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:52.090
with people who might
sometimes be litigious

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:53.900
without putting themselves at legal risk.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:56.010
- I can't imagine that you ever run

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:58.900
into these kind of issues on YouTube.

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:00.370
- This is purely hypothetical.

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:01.908
- Absolutely understandable.

00:02:01.908 --> 00:02:05.520
None of us have ever run
into these kind of issues.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:06.870
Well it's interesting from my perspective

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:09.450
is that the US and the UK

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:12.020
have very different defamation laws

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:14.342
when it comes to talking about individuals

00:02:14.342 --> 00:02:18.840
and corporations and where the line is

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:20.420
in terms of what is commentary

00:02:20.420 --> 00:02:22.080
and what crosses the line

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:24.200
into a defamatory statement.
- [Harry] Hmm.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.120
- And traditionally
there's been a difference

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.270
between libel which is written

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:30.390
and slander which is spoken.

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:32.410
And these days that distinction

00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:33.830
doesn't really matter anymore.

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:34.840
As an American lawyer

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:36.210
I'm not an expert in the UK

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:38.070
but what I can tell you is that

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:39.260
in the US at least

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:40.120
when you are talking

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:42.682
about these kind of commentary issues

00:02:42.682 --> 00:02:44.640
where you run into defamation.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:45.860
The key is that

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:47.210
defamation only applies

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:49.550
to a provable statement of fact

00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:51.080
that is false.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:53.462
So most people know that

00:02:53.462 --> 00:02:54.960
at least in the US

00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:56.310
and this is not true in all countries

00:02:56.310 --> 00:02:59.510
that truth is a defense to defamation.

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:01.110
But the underlying statement itself

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:04.230
has to be a provable statement of fact.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:05.904
So it can't be an opinion,

00:03:05.904 --> 00:03:08.250
it can't be hyperbole,

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:12.430
it can't be ridiculousness and parody.

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:14.110
There's a famous case in the US

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:17.320
where the pornographic magazine Penthouse

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:18.630
owned by Larry Flint

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:21.212
did a spread about Jerry Falwell

00:03:21.212 --> 00:03:22.970
losing his virginity

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:25.140
and all the ridiculous
hijinks that ensued.

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:27.047
And he sued for defamatory purposes.

00:03:27.047 --> 00:03:28.915
- [Harry] Mmm-hmm.
- [Host] And the court held

00:03:28.915 --> 00:03:31.030
basically as a matter of law

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:32.230
that it was so ridiculous

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:33.440
that no one would've believed

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:34.750
that A, Jerry Falwell

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:36.242
gave this interview to Penthouse

00:03:36.242 --> 00:03:39.790
and B, that he actually did these things

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:42.230
in the course of losing his virginity.

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:43.260
- Hmm.
- [Host] So really

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:44.880
the more ridiculous something is

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:47.430
that almost becomes more of a defense.

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:50.400
Even when you start edging into the realm

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.060
of things that are factual in nature.

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:53.900
At least on YouTube

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:55.837
the kind of commentary
that you see most often

00:03:55.837 --> 00:03:59.490
is things that are people's opinion.

00:03:59.490 --> 00:04:02.710
You might call someone
a jerk or much worse

00:04:02.710 --> 00:04:04.120
but it's really when you get

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:08.170
into these discrete pieces
of factual information

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:09.915
that are factually wrong

00:04:09.915 --> 00:04:12.110
that you have an issue.

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:14.520
And I don't know if you're familiar

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:17.388
with the extra standard of celebrity.

00:04:17.388 --> 00:04:19.880
But in the US

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:22.420
if you are someone of notoriety

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:23.944
and a certain amount of celebrity

00:04:23.944 --> 00:04:25.730
you actually have to show

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:26.563
that the person

00:04:26.563 --> 00:04:28.939
when they made the false statement of fact

00:04:28.939 --> 00:04:30.715
that they knew it was false

00:04:30.715 --> 00:04:32.360
and they said it

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:34.548
with what's called malicious intent.

00:04:34.548 --> 00:04:36.979
So that becomes even more difficult

00:04:36.979 --> 00:04:38.820
when you're talking about

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:41.505
say politicians, or famous billionaires.

00:04:41.505 --> 00:04:43.930
- I can see now why certain politicians

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:45.687
will cover themselves by saying

00:04:45.687 --> 00:04:47.140
"Well to the best of my knowledge"

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:48.480
so they're not obviously lying.

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:49.910
Or they'll only provide facts

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:51.460
that support their beliefs.

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:52.940
Just those facts.

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:53.773
And they're not lying

00:04:53.773 --> 00:04:54.900
they're just only showing

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:57.090
very careful versions of the truth.

00:04:57.090 --> 00:04:57.923
- Right exactly.

00:04:57.923 --> 00:05:01.630
And you know, even in the
context of politicians,

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:04.340
we've seen several defamation lawsuits

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:06.160
against President Trump at the moment.

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:08.290
He is currently in a lawsuit

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:10.900
with a woman named Summer Zervos

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:14.090
who has said that the
president defamed her

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:16.470
by saying that he did not engage

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:18.290
in certain sexual activities with her

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:20.270
and called her a liar.

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:21.620
That's going to be somewhat

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:23.060
of a groundbreaking lawsuit

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:25.090
because it's gonna be a question

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:27.150
of whether she's a private person

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:28.300
or someone of note.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:31.390
Whether the president is
a private person or not.

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:33.660
I mean usually they are
not considered private.

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:35.238
They have that amount of celebrity.

00:05:35.238 --> 00:05:36.071
- Yeah yeah.

00:05:36.071 --> 00:05:37.250
- [Host] And whether his statement

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:39.078
of saying that she was a liar

00:05:39.078 --> 00:05:42.170
is something that is a
provable statement of fact

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:45.100
or whether it's hyperbole and an opinion.

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:46.000
- I remember a suit where

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:47.260
do you know Jim Sterling?

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:48.093
- I do yes.

00:05:48.093 --> 00:05:49.740
- [Harry] He was sued for $15 million

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:50.850
or something by someone

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:53.000
on the account of libel slander

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:53.833
various stuff like that.

00:05:53.833 --> 00:05:54.850
It was an equivalent sort of suit

00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:55.840
and one of the things they listed

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:57.480
as one of the grievances

00:05:57.480 --> 00:05:58.313
was at some point he said

00:05:58.313 --> 00:06:00.400
"There's not enough popcorn in the world

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:01.770
to sort of laugh at this person

00:06:01.770 --> 00:06:03.580
for how dumb they're being".

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:04.770
And this was put in the suit

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:06.600
as a quote as one of the grievances.

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:07.433
- Yeah.

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:08.950
- So and one of the things
they considered doing

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:10.710
is challenging to prove

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:12.830
that there wasn't enough
popcorn in the world.

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:14.130
- I'm guessing that Jim Sterling

00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:15.600
probably won that lawsuit.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:16.820
- It got dropped with prejudice

00:06:16.820 --> 00:06:17.653
I believe in the end.

00:06:17.653 --> 00:06:18.590
- [Host] Okay yeah.

00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:20.080
If it was dismissed by the court

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:21.960
on the substance of the issue

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:23.920
then likely they can't bring it up again.

00:06:23.920 --> 00:06:25.730
- Oh good that's good to hear.

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:27.472
Sometimes I make factual statements

00:06:27.472 --> 00:06:29.540
and then because we're not perfect

00:06:29.540 --> 00:06:30.460
you discover later

00:06:30.460 --> 00:06:32.010
that some of the facts you mentioned

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:33.509
are themselves selective

00:06:33.509 --> 00:06:36.280
or mistakes or wrong.

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:37.450
In which case I have

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:38.832
in a sense told a lie.

00:06:38.832 --> 00:06:40.510
Is there a legal precedent

00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:42.740
for someone saying a falsehood

00:06:42.740 --> 00:06:43.573
and getting in trouble

00:06:43.573 --> 00:06:44.797
for saying it

00:06:44.797 --> 00:06:45.630
even if they believed it at the time?

00:06:45.630 --> 00:06:47.340
- Well that's a great question

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:50.920
and partially hinges on the nature

00:06:50.920 --> 00:06:53.630
of the person that is spoken about.

00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:55.170
There's no cause of action

00:06:55.170 --> 00:06:57.970
for just saying a falsehood in public.

00:06:57.970 --> 00:06:59.820
Defamation applies to when you are

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:01.860
directing a false statement of fact

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:03.130
towards an individual person

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:04.430
that harms their reputation.

00:07:04.430 --> 00:07:06.400
So an innocent mistake

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:09.140
of merely saying something
that was incorrect

00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:10.910
but you thought it to be true.

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:12.970
If you're talking about someone

00:07:12.970 --> 00:07:16.050
that is a celebrity or of note

00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:18.830
likely that is not grounds for defamation

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:20.915
because you have to meet that extra hurdle

00:07:20.915 --> 00:07:24.320
to get into the actual malice standard

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:25.550
when you're talking about a celebrity.

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:26.950
- I see that's great.

00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:28.250
One more question.
- [Host] Please.

00:07:28.250 --> 00:07:29.670
- I have a question about the definition

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:31.440
if there's a proper legal definition

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:33.600
of the concept of being libel-proof.

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:35.540
In the sort of anime voice acting scene

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:38.090
there's currently a spurious lawsuit

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:39.490
by a certain voice actor

00:07:39.490 --> 00:07:40.323
against the company

00:07:40.323 --> 00:07:41.730
for supposed libel.

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:43.730
And the counterargument
the company's making

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:47.070
is that this person is
effectively impossible

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:48.610
to do libel towards

00:07:48.610 --> 00:07:51.790
because they have done
so many other things

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:52.690
that at this point

00:07:52.690 --> 00:07:54.170
it's barely making anything up

00:07:54.170 --> 00:07:55.480
to assert certain things.

00:07:55.480 --> 00:07:58.413
- Yes so that it a potential defense.

00:08:00.150 --> 00:08:01.048
The court can find

00:08:01.048 --> 00:08:04.715
what would normally be
a defamatory statement

00:08:04.715 --> 00:08:06.780
is not defamatory in this context

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:08.650
because the reputation is so bad--

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:09.483
- Hmm.

00:08:09.483 --> 00:08:10.592
- [Host] It can't get any worse.

00:08:10.592 --> 00:08:11.425
- (laughs)

00:08:11.425 --> 00:08:12.930
- Harry, thank you so much

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:15.230
for joining this episode

00:08:15.230 --> 00:08:16.580
of the yet to be named

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:18.140
Legal Eagle interview show.

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:18.973
- Thank you for having me.

00:08:18.973 --> 00:08:20.180
- [Host] And if you could

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:22.600
pass the information along to AOC

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:24.500
and we'll get her on the hot seat

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:25.580
